  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=\u27e8{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}\u27e9$ and $f(x,y)=2x,$ calculate $\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,\u2207\\cdot F+F\\cdot \u2207f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\u2207\\cdot F$ and $\u2207f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f & =\u27e82,0\u27e9, \\\\ \u2207\\cdot F & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({e}^{3x})+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(-2y{e}^{3x})=3{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x}={e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,\u2207\\cdot F+F\\cdot \u2207f \\\\  & =2x({e}^{3x})+\u27e8{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =2x{e}^{3x}+2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
